**Issue**: #413
**Date**: 2026-09-23
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG

Feature: Recover external-only incomplete verification after prerequisite returns

  @AC1 @AC2
  Scenario: A single exact owner can recheck external evidence
    Given an approved singular issue spec and unchanged registered verification identity
    And a valid Incomplete report and complete exact-head artifact with only external required incomplete results
    When the same verify owner begins recovery
    Then one durable attempt is consumed before the registered gate runs
    And a second invocation for that owner cannot rerun the gate

  @AC1 @AC4
  Scenario: Unsafe or changed evidence never receives a recovery attempt
    Given an Incomplete report with stale head, changed spec or config, malformed coverage, unsafe artifact, or required failed result
    When verification is reinvoked
    Then no external recovery attempt is consumed
    And normal publication-only finalization remains intervention-bearing

  @AC3
  Scenario: An available prerequisite produces fresh passing evidence
    Given the exact candidate and an external prerequisite now available
    When the registered gate reruns and all required applicable validations pass
    Then verification regenerates and publishes an accurate report through normal finalization
    And execute advances only after its passed handoff

  @AC3 @AC4
  Scenario: An unavailable prerequisite does not become a pass
    Given the exact candidate and an external prerequisite still unavailable
    When the one-use registered gate reruns and remains Incomplete
    Then the historical report is preserved without forged publication or handoff
    And execute remains blocked without an automatic retry
